OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Fri 31 Jul to Sun 9 Aug
OL,6,FMostly dry away from the north and
OL,7,Fnorthwest where scattered showers are
OL,8,Fexpected. There is a small chance that
OL,9,Fsome other western parts could see
OL,10,Fsome rain by the end of the weekend.
OL,11,FTemperatures ranging from around
OL,12,Faverage in the NW to warm in the
OL,13,Fsoutheast, perhaps becoming very warm
OL,14,Fin the southeast through the weekend.
OL,15,FIt will probably become more
OL,16,Fchangeable thereafter, with potential
OL,17,Ffor an area of low pressure to move
OL,18,Fclose to or across the UK early in
OL,19,FAugust. This could bring spells of
OL,20,Fheavy rain and perhaps some strong
OL,21,Fwinds for a time. It may become more
OL,22,Fsettled again toward the end of the
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,23,Ffirst week of August.
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
FL,164,160,301,260,100,100
PN,16303
SC,0003
CT,20,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F163A1785073676
OL,1,Wj5hw1~{4k7juhw1{$             G3/3
OL,2,W+.-'"-$/*%*%*%/"-$/*%Q,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Mon 10 Aug to Mon 24 Aug
OL,6,FDry and settled conditions will
OL,7,Fprobably dominate much of this period
OL,8,Fwith high pressure patterns tending to
OL,9,Faffect the UK. This may be interrupted
OL,10,Fat times by Atlantic frontal systems,
OL,11,Fespecially in the north, or
OL,12,Fthunderstorms in the south. However,
OL,13,Foverall rainfall amounts will likely
OL,14,Fbe below normal. Temperatures will
OL,15,Fprobably be above normal and some
OL,16,Fspells of hot weather and heatwaves
OL,17,Fare possible, especially in the south.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
